course: dictionary
lesson: 6753
title: Onward: going on, and after
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Onward means forward, going further on. Look for it in the words around it. «Onward they marched» tells you they kept going, not that they stopped or turned back.
explain: Onward also means from a time and later. In «from the Han period onward», the words from and later are the clues. The Silk Road trade routes were linked from that time and kept going after it.
explain: You can swap in a simple word to check your meaning. Try «from then on» or «going forward» in place of onward. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Onward means forward, going further on.
fact: «From Monday onward» means from Monday, and then after it.
fact: An onward journey is the next part of a trip.
fact: Onwards means the same as onward when it is used for time or direction.
fact: You can check by swapping in «from then on», «going forward» or «and after».
exercise: In «from the Han period onward», what does onward mean? | Upside down | Backwards, back to the past | *From that time on, and after | Only for a short time
exercise: «Onward they marched through the snow.» What does onward tell you? | They turned around and went home | *They kept going forward | They ran away and hid | They stopped and sat down
exercise: Which phrase shows a rule that starts at a point and goes on after it? | *From age 5 onwards | Very quickly | Yesterday | Under the table
test: Ella's flight is an onward flight, so it is | The first part of the trip | *The next part of the trip | A flight that is cancelled | The last flight ever
test: Mum says the rule starts «from Monday onward». When does the rule begin? | Monday was yesterday | Only on Sunday | *On Monday, and it keeps going after that | Never
exam: Which sentence uses onward to mean going further on? | The cake was onward on the plate | *They walked onward through the forest, past the river and up the hill | Onward is a colour of paint | The bus stopped here
